### Self-issued JWT auth flow.
### Set @host to the API's current port (the VS Docker port is ephemeral - check `docker ps`).
@host = http://localhost:62945
@username = rider
@password = dev-only-password-change-me

### 1. Get a JWT
# @name token
POST {{host}}/auth/token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "{{username}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### 2. Save a .fit file - authorized (expect 201 Created)
POST {{host}}/files/fit?rideDate=2026-06-08T08:00:00Z
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=BoundaryFit

--BoundaryFit
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="fit"; filename="ride.fit"
Content-Type: application/octet-stream

sample fit file bytes
--BoundaryFit--

### 3. Save a .fit file - no token (expect 401 Unauthorized)
POST {{host}}/files/fit?rideDate=2026-06-08T08:00:00Z
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=BoundaryFit

--BoundaryFit
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="fit"; filename="ride.fit"
Content-Type: application/octet-stream

sample fit file bytes
--BoundaryFit--
